# The environment the suite of this application boots its kernel in (issue beffroi-auth/beffroi#521). Loaded
# only when APP_ENV is test, and ".env.local" is not read at all in that environment, so a run here never
# takes a value a desk or a stack wrote: what is not here comes from ".env" and from nothing else.
#
# A real environment variable still wins over this file, which is what lets the same suite run on the
# machine, where "castor app-phpunit" hands it the database of the stack, and on a runner, where the
# service container answers on the loopback address ".env" already names.

###> symfony/framework-bundle ###
KERNEL_CLASS='App\Kernel'
# The secret of a kernel that signs nothing anybody outside this process will read. It is a fixture, as
# every value below is: what a deployment runs on is its own, and nothing here is ever deployed.
APP_SECRET='$ecretf0rt3st'
###< symfony/framework-bundle ###

###> beffroi/symfony-bundle ###
# The issuer the pages of the suite are served under. The host answers nowhere: a functional test sends its
# requests into the kernel and no socket is opened.
BEFFROI_ISSUER=https://op.test
# The KMS that seals the keys of the tenant and the data keys its personal columns are sealed under
# (decisions 0011 and 0018). A test that writes a person writes sealed columns, so a kernel with no KMS
# could not create one at all: the sodium backend with a key inline in this file is what the suite runs on,
# as the test kernel of the bundle does, and it is the one place of this repository where a key is written
# down. It seals the rows of a database the suite drops before every test and nothing else, and the
# deployment reads its own DSN from an environment that is not this file.
BEFFROI_KMS_DSN="sodium://?keys[test]=IEZfUrlrJUy_yqaAEBw1sBCvlMXG1ZNmlwllU1onw-I"
BEFFROI_KMS_KEY_ID=test
###< beffroi/symfony-bundle ###

###> beffroi/op ###
# The secrets of the clients the demonstration plays a flow as (issue #462), fixtures like every value
# above: the suite has no provider to call, so no request ever carries one, and what a test reads of a
# drawn hop is the request the demonstration built. The subject a backchannel flow names its user by is
# one too, "castor provision" writing the real one into a file this environment does not read.
DEMO_SERVICE_SECRET='service-secret-of-at-least-32-characters-l'
DEMO_CIBA_POLL_SECRET='backchannel-secret-of-at-least-32-characte'
BEFFROI_DEV_USER_SUBJECT='alice-subject'
###< beffroi/op ###
